(footprint "TO-264-3_Vertical_HS657-10ABPE"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "TO-264-3 vertical transistor (RM 5.45mm, MJL21193/MJL21194) bolted to a Wakefield 657-10ABPE vertical board-mount heat sink (extrusion 6533 - symmetric fin profile with a central mounting web; identical base/pad/pin pattern for all 657-10/15/20/25ABPE; the -10 = 1in/25.4mm tall variant is used to fit the 100x160 Eurocard). The device bolts to the CENTRAL WEB (0.144in/3.7mm hole THRU, 21.6mm up the vertical face) so the transistor sits centred in the 25.4mm heat-sink depth, NOT on the front face. Combined footprint (origin = device centre lead): pads 1/2/3 = device B/C/E (drill 1.5mm) at the depth-centre of the sink; two unnamed plated pads = heat-sink wave-solder pins (0.093in/2.4mm dia on 1.000in/25.4mm centres across the 41.9mm width, symmetric about the device). Heat-sink base 41.9 x 25.4mm, centred on the device leads. Pad pitch and pin span are exact; the pins are drawn coplanar with the device lead row (depth Y=0) - VERIFY the exact pin-row depth against the physical part before fabrication. Thermal 6.8 C/W natural (41C@6W), 3.7 C/W @ 200 LFM. Isolate device tab from sink with an insulating thermal pad (Same Sky/Wakefield WTI7R1F0-1.00X0.75) plus a #4 shoulder washer (Boyd 7721-7PPSG) on the mounting bolt. Per-device dissipation ~4.5W avg (fan-cooled Tj ~69C) per v3 power analysis.")
	(tags "TO-264 TO-247 heatsink 657-10ABPE Wakefield vertical MJL21193 MJL21194 power pass transistor")
